## Status Command

Give a brief status report of the current session. Include:

1. **Task** — what we are working on (goal, feature, bug)
2. **Done** — what has been completed so far (list changed/created files with one-line description each)
3. **Current state** — does the code compile? are there known issues?
4. **Next** — what remains to be done, in priority order

Run `git diff --stat` to get the actual list of changed files. Keep the report concise — no filler, no redundancy. Write in the same language the user has been using in this conversation.
